  "notes": "Image 1: 'Busy' is printed for pins used elsewhere and is kept as the label. Image 6 (14683b71) is an 'Advanced Section' warning page with no connectors. Images 2 and 4 combine diagram labels (Nano name + ESP32 number) with board silkscreen (B0/B1, RX0/TX1, 3.3V, VBUS, RST). Image 7 note on D1/TX0: 'WARNING D1/TX0 pin has a 499 ohm resistor in series and therefore the maximum current is limited'. Image 8 bottom view: QSPI flash lines (top view) point to the flash chip, not header pins, and are skipped; bottom-view header holes only carry battery/VBUS callouts (3V3, GND, SJ1 solder jumper, VBUS) and are not transcribed as a row. RGB LED, LED_BUILTIN and Power LED skipped."
